          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>\"Iron Chancellor\"</strong><br>\nBismarck was known as the \"Iron Chancellor\" for his strong leadership and political astuteness. He established the political structure that allowed the Kaiser to rule while he effectively controlled German policy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Social Reforms</strong><br>\nBismarck implemented progressive social reforms, such as health insurance and pensions, to appease the working class and stave off socialist revolution in a newly united Germany.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Foreign Policy</strong><br>\nHis foreign policy aimed at securing Germany's position as a great European power while maintaining peace through a complex system of alliances with other European countries.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
