            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Bismarck's Downfall</strong><br>\nHis fall from power came after Emperor Wilhelm II ascended to the throne in 1888. The young Kaiser opposed Bismarck's careful foreign policy, leading to the chancellor's resignation in 1890.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Final Years</strong><br>\nAfter his resignation, Bismarck retired to his estate in Varzin. He published his reflections and engaged in frequent correspondence, reflecting on his political life and decisions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nOtto von Bismarck died on July 30, 1898. His legacy as the founder of the German Empire and as a master strategist in domestic and foreign affairs remains a significant part of German history.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
